.claude/plans/PLAN-177/repass-rc4-20260816-t6-GWC-superseded/transcript-rc4-1.log:7699:Concrete failure scenario: the filter identifies probes solely by five missing metadata fields; it never checks the probe description or prompt. `subagent_type` is optional under the payload contract. Therefore an actual event such as “Review production authentication” with those optional/derived fields absent is discarded as a harness probe, hiding precisely the unclassified spawn the ratio is intended to expose.
.claude/plans/PLAN-177/repass-rc4-20260816-t6-GWC-superseded/transcript-rc4-1.log:7701:Minimal fix: require a positive harness fingerprint—an explicit discriminator, or a tightly closed description/prompt signature. Add a negative control using an arbitrary real description with all five metadata fields absent.
