.claude/plans/PLAN-177/repass-rc4-20260816-t6-GWC-superseded/transcript-rc4-2.log:8075:./SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:487:| `codex_review_verdict` (v2.52) | `action`, `outcome` (str — CLOSED enum: `clean` / `findings` / `skipped_failopen` / `detected_only`; an unrecognized value is COERCED to `skipped_failopen` — never to a healthy-class value, so unparseable telemetry input can never claim rail health), `diff_sha256` (str — 64-lowercase-hex sha256 of the reviewed assembled risky diff, shape-validated; any off-shape value COERCED to `""`), `session_id` (threaded from the Stop-hook stdin event, fallback `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` env, then `""`), `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-161 W2 C5 / CF-9 (2026-07-27) — Stop-hook cross-model review OUTCOME, emitted by `codex_review_user_code.py` once per distinct (`diff_sha256`, `outcome`) pair (telemetry dedupe SEPARATE from the review-status dedupe, so Stop-retry loops re-review without re-emitting). `clean`/`findings` require a strictly PARSED verdict (bounded `- <file>: <issue>` grammar or exact `CLEAN`); infra fail-open (codex missing / rc!=0 / empty stdout / timeout) AND malformed output both map to `skipped_failopen`; DETECT-ONLY default mode maps its nudge to `detected_only` (neutral). Feeds the /ceo-boot `failopen_rail_liveness_7d` `stop_review` sub-rail. Typed emitter `emit_codex_review_verdict`; dedicated deny-by-default `_CODEX_REVIEW_VERDICT_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch + VALUE re-coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the verdict TEXT, the diff content, file paths (a Codex finding can quote secrets from the reviewed diff). Deliberately NOT `pair_rail_codex_unavailable` — that action feeds the dispatcher's Codex-outage predicate and must stay unpolluted. NO ATLAS technique (liveness telemetry, not a detection signal). |
