   ```

   They return no noncanonical lines, count one decision, and resolve it as `GO`. Using the otherwise-live rc.4 envelope, the server validator printed `OK` and exited 0. A root-list line such as `- verdict: NO-GO` is likewise accepted. These are malformed YAML, so accepting them violates the fail-closed-on-input rule. The regression matrix omits both states.

   Minimal fix: track whether an indented line has an active bare parent; reject orphan indentation and root-level list items. Add both shapes to the cross-reader matrix and full validator/tag-guard controls.

