   Concrete failure: `currently 1.0.1 <!-- last-reviewed: 2026-08-05 v1.3.0 -->` is skipped wholesale because the line contains a valid stamp. The positive control places the stale literal and stamp on separate lines, so it misses this bypass.

   Minimal fix: remove only the stamp substring before scanning the remainder, and add a same-line relapse fixture.

